### 1. Same name as an existing product (expect 201, slug "red-shoes-2")
POST http://localhost:3000/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Red Shoes",
  "price": 3499,
  "stock": 5,
  "categoryId": 4
}

### 2. Custom slug gets cleaned (expect 201, slug "my-custom-slug")
POST http://localhost:3000/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Dress",
  "slug": "My Custom Slug!",
  "price": 5000,
  "stock": 1,
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 3. Rename keeps the slug (expect slug still "my-custom-slug")
PATCH http://localhost:3000/products/32
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Renamed Dress"
}

### 4. Name without letters or digits (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "!!!",
  "price": 100,
  "stock": 1,
  "categoryId": 1
}